    "raw": "{\"ruleId\":\"item-0ad918526bc9\",\"class\":\"expressible\",\"constraints\":[{\"id\":\"domain-no-app\",\"type\":\"forbiddenDependency\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"to\":\"module:src/app/**\",\"scopePaths\":[\"src/domain/**\"]}],\"coverage\":\"Every direct import edge from a module under src/domain to a module under src/app in the post-change tree. This covers import, import type, export ... from and import(). An import from src/domain that the checker cannot resolve also fails, which errs on the strict side.\",\"residual\":null,\"probes\":{\"violating\":{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/src/domain/leak.ts b/src/domain/leak.ts\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/domain/leak.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@\\n+import { placeOrder } from \\\"../app/place-order\\\";\\n+export const usePlaceOrder = placeOrder;\\n\"},\"compliant\":{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/src/domain/vat.ts b/src/domain/vat.ts\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/domain/vat.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\\n+export const VAT_RATE = 0.21;\\n\"}},\"rationale\":\"The rule is a structural layering constraint between two directory globs. The checker's import graph covers static imports, type imports, re-exports and dynamic imports, so one forbiddenDependency from src/domain/** to src/app/** decides it mechanically. No meaning or intent is involved.\"}",
